{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/12/codegen_prompts/2.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/12`\n- 题号：`2`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed56627177/12/2.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"2\">\n- `description`：将网格中每个多色精灵按其内部颜色层数进行\"剥洋葱\"式分解，从外到内逐层提取轮廓并按从左到右的顺序排列在输出网格中。\n- `Input structure`：背景为 black。网格中有若干个独立的多色精灵（互不接触），每个精灵由 2 到 4 种颜色组成，呈同心嵌套结构——最外层是一种颜色，向内每层换一种颜色，类似靶心图案（但形状不一定是矩形，可以是不规则的 4-连通区域，只要每层完整包裹内层即可）。每个精灵的层数可能不同。\n- `Rule`：对每个精灵，从最外层开始逐层\"剥离\"——第一层是精灵最外圈像素构成的轮廓（即与背景 4-连通相邻的像素），第二层是去掉最外层后新暴露的外圈像素，依此类推，直到最内层核心。将每一层单独提取出来（保持其相对空间位置），按照从外到内的顺序从左到右排列在输出网格中，层与层之间用一列背景色分隔。每层只保留该层自身颜色的像素，其余位置为背景色。精灵之间的排列顺序按照它们在输入网格中从上到下、从左到右的出现顺序，精灵之间用两列背景色分隔。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先识别每个精灵的同心嵌套层级结构，再理解\"剥离\"的顺序是从外向内逐层提取轮廓。两个非显然的推理步骤：（1）判断哪些像素属于同一\"层\"（即当前最外圈），（2）理解输出中各层的排列顺序编码了原精灵的嵌套深度。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/d749d46f, eval/dbff022c, train/465b7d93, train/b71a7747, eval/581f7754, train/ac6f9922, train/db615bd4, train/538b439f\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d749d46f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3571\nmechanism=0.4510\nlexical=0.0121\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/d749d46f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms\nseparate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.\n\nRule\nBuild a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width of the wide\nversions of the rectangles. For each source rectangle, paint a top-aligned\nrectangle of shape min(h,w) by max(h,w), with one background column between\nconsecutive rectangles. Then, starting again from the left edge, paint a\nbottom-aligned rectangle of shape max(h,w) by min(h,w) for each source rectangle,\nagain separated by one background column.\n\nKey insight\nThe input rectangles are not copied in their original orientations; each object\ncontributes one horizontal-facing and one vertical-facing normalized rectangle,\npreserving left-to-right object order.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"solid monochromatic foreground rectangles ordered left-to-right\",\n  \"dst\": \"packed upper wide slots and lower tall slots in the same left-to-right order\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"rank(s) == rank(d) for both the upper and lower slot sequences\",\n  \"transform\": \"paint each rectangle twice: min(h,w) by max(h,w) top-aligned in the upper band, and max(h,w) by min(h,w) bottom-aligned in the lower band, with one background column between slots\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"height 10; width is the sum of max(h,w) over source rectangles plus one separator column between consecutive rectangles\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3369\nmechanism=0.3862\nlexical=0.0117\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"465b7d93\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3311\nmechanism=0.3950\nlexical=0.0122\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:rectangle, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/465b7d93.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/465b7d93.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the small colored sprite into the hollow frame by stretching its shape to the frame interior.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly two foreground colors: one forms a complete rectangular\n  one-pixel-thick frame, and the other forms one 4-connected sprite outside it.\n- The frame interior is initially background.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the original sprite from its outside location.\n- Map the sprite bbox to the frame interior bbox, sending bbox extremes to\n  interior extremes.\n- Draw straight horizontal or vertical segments between mapped positions of\n  adjacent sprite pixels, then fill any enclosed background region inside\n  those drawn segments.\n\nKey insight:\nThe outside sprite is a miniature line/fill diagram for the frame interior,\nnot a bitmap to scale by block replication.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"small colored sprite s outside the frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"hollow rectangular frame interior d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"unique s maps to unique d; s.bbox extremes align to d.bbox extremes\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear s; stretch s into d by mapping bbox extremes, drawing 4-adjacent segments, and filling enclosed regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b71a7747\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3381\nmechanism=0.4582\nlexical=0.0128\ncode_feature=0.2000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:axis, object:rectangle, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/b71a7747.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b71a7747.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExtract the hidden two-color image by compacting the rows and columns of its complete mask.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid contains one pair of colors whose pixels occupy every cell in the\ncross product of their active rows and active columns; all other colors form\nthe surrounding filler or separators.\nRule\nFind that unique color pair, keep exactly the rows and columns touched by\nthe pair, and return the induced subgrid.\nKey insight\nThe target image is not chosen by color id; it is the only two-color mask\nwhose occupied pixels form a full rectangular row/column product after\ndeleting unused rows and columns.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"unique two-color mask whose pixels fill the cross product of its active rows and active columns\",\n  \"transform\": \"delete every row and column not touched by that mask, preserving the induced two-color subgrid\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"active mask rows x active mask columns\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3526\nmechanism=0.4266\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:sprite, operation:sort_order, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
